editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:25:- **The council, the second honest collision:** Lira for walking away (the fence at forty and the walk at fifty, and pace the third circle on their own time); Brom ("Three hundred's a number a man doesn't reach for." — his father and the horse); Karis ("I would go alone."); **Seln: "Take it… People have faces. Six years I've wanted a face."** Cael's sentence to the whole table (protected), then why: the assumption is wrong and cannot be known to be wrong. **Brom quotes Rooke**, the first person he has ever quoted: "Doors open both ways… I don't like it. I'm in." Lira: "I want it entered that I said walk away." The log (EXC-B7-002). Pike marks HOLD unasked and says it to the room. **Teague at the door** (protected): "If you're late back, we'll come look." / "Noted.", the first *Noted* to anyone above them on the wall.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:32:- **Lowmarch (129–131):** the fifth honest catalogue, from the landing. **The season line read** (protected); the ledger turned toward him; **no number**; "too small" (protected); the room's "Eleventh." / "Aye." **Teague's term** and "Noted." The healer's single look at Brom's shoulder. **The winter fence** given over ("Ours."). Karis takes the back room and pays without counting (ninety-six). **The inventory** (protected; the audio rule). **The last ferry**: nine pieces sorted aloud; **Hesk's straightedge** with the note (protected); the replies west (protected). **Oryn's letter by carter** the morning after (protected): "Six, by letter." "She'll say when." / "Spring." **The map**: four circles, the bearing, both edges laid along it, **touching the three paced centres for Cael exactly as for Karis**. "The sites were on an alignment. Not random." "Someone made this pattern." Four seconds. **The closing, exact.**
editions/monroe-1.3/tools/sol_recheck.sh:19:Read the FULL current movement, then follow $E/tools/RECHECK-TEMPLATE.md exactly: (1) brief items RESOLVED/PARTIAL/NOT with quoted evidence (diff -U0 vs pre-repair); (2) continuity; (3) formula — run \`python3 $E/tools/formula_metrics.py\` on the chapters, \`bash $E/tools/ed.sh overlap $B $N\`, \`bash $E/tools/ed.sh gates $B $N\`, \`bash $E/tools/sweep_probe.sh $B $N $N\`; (4) reader clarity; (5) listening proof on every chapter.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:23:- **The cascade: it listens, it doesn't pull (three nights).** His own current at the edge of every thought; the nine coming up out of it one at a time and told apart by sound; "a room he had lived in for eighteen years with the lights suddenly on." Brom on the ladder ("How many people." / "Nine. Ten. I can't hear the tenth. It's the thing I'm hearing with." / the forge story). Day two: **Storm heard resettling** in the yard, a hand on the well's rim; the ground arriving half a beat late under a counted foot, so he **relearns the Wind economy in the yard** while the listening runs (a learning encounter). **Oryn's "Where is it loudest."** "Here… It's not louder there. It's nearer." Ask first, said in the yard: "I ask the dying." / "I ask first. Every time."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:45:The sensation-language of listening, kept to sensation; Thornwater in the back of autumn (ice on the trough, the grain going up the ladder past where they sleep); the tables' daily rhythm; the bowman's manner and words; the birthday's warmth and humor; the shape of each finding scene; all the windows.
