editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:238:## 10. Protected wording (verbatim; later books quote or call these back)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:240:Callbacks confirmed in Book 8's closed prose: Oryn's letter and "Find me at Thornwater." / "Bring the map." (B8 Ch1, Ch24); "a tape and a season" (B8 Ch1); "Lie still when I say" (B8 Ch18, Ch24); Brom's "Twice… not three times this season" (B8 Ch6); "A measurement is a fact about a ruler, not about the hand that held it." (B8 Ch1, Ch5, Ch20); Hesk's "true to a hair" / "draw a line through it" / "Mind the shape" (B8 Ch1, Ch17, Ch18, Ch22, Ch24); "too small" (B8 Ch16, Ch17, Ch24); "Stop touching it." (B8 Ch7); "Not the Quiet." (B8 Ch7, Ch24); "He'll speak to you when you've cost him something" (B8 Ch7); Teague's spring term (B8 Ch1, Ch17); "Eleventh" (B8 Ch1, Ch12, Ch17); "the Bronze from Ardenmere" (B8 Ch7); ninety-six in hand (B8 Ch1); fifty-two sheets and forty-one kinds (B8 Ch9–11). Canon documents quote "Three points make a line. Four make an argument.", "Someone made this pattern.", the looms finding, "A circle is a made shape." and the stratum limit. Every other item below is a signature line or document of this book. **Keep them all exact.** Speaker attributions may be re-staged; the words may not.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:269:- **Oryn's letter (Ch24):** *Route's whole. The knee held. Nobody died of three weeks. Spring: bring the map, and lie still when I say. — O.* — then: Six, by letter. (The architecture and series docs still quote "eleven days"; prose and Book 8 say **three weeks**. See C6.)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:288:- Ch17 (EXC-B7-002): *Priced too well. Seln says it's for the case. I say the floor's for me and they don't know it. South, tomorrow. Lira's arm is two weeks old. Brom says doors open both ways. He's quoting Rooke. He's never quoted anyone.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:355:- **C6 · Oryn's lateness and the letter.** Ch12's "The route's eleven days north of here" and Ch15's "nine days late here and eleven at the next" do not reconcile (seams F5a, accepted as spoken). Ch18 projects Thornwater "eleven days late"; the closed prose then says **three weeks** at the fork (Ch23) and in the letter (Ch24), and Book 8 Ch1 quotes "Nobody died of three weeks." The architecture card and `series/THE_FRACTURED_PATH_SERIES.md` still say "eleven days." **The edition protects "three weeks."** Recommend writing Ch12's figure as a distance ("the far end of the route is eleven days north of here") and keeping the lateness arithmetic honest from day 104 (nine and eleven) to day 110 (Oxhollow seventeen) to the fork (three weeks).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:372:**By-ear watch list for the audiobook (carried from the registry):** Feryn and Oryn never in one list run ("the Bronze from Ardenmere"); the Oryn / Oxhollow / Ostrand O-stack; Pike / Fiske; Stair / (Book 8's) Span. Avoid putting Oxhollow and Oryn in one short sentence where it can be helped.
