editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-003/compiled-prompt.md:614:The first page set out the provision. It did so accurately. It quoted the half page Cael had read more times than he had counted in the archive, and then explained, in plain sentences, what the provision was for: the academic exposure and supervised training of candidates who had not yet undergone formal Kindling assessment, which was to say, in nearly every case, children. It noted that such candidates were assessed monthly by demonstration, and that the standard was consistent, observable practice. It observed, correctly, that a child who had not yet Kindled would ordinarily have very little to practise.
