editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:341:## 10. Protected wording (verbatim; canon quotes or calls back these, or Book 9 inherits them)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:343:Tier A is quoted in the canon files (bible, ledger, series entry) or is a system notice. Tier B is wording from earlier books that this book quotes; it is binding from its own book. Tier C is fixed by the source architecture as closers or fixed lines; keep it verbatim, because Book 9's planning will read the source. Straight quotes and em dashes as in the source; italics are not wording.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:345:### Tier A — canon-quoted and system text
