editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/recheck-r1.md:52:**ch42 scene 3 (office, door, stair, aide) — new prose.** Own entry (Coss mid-sentence; Cael counting the room: four chairs, three taken, the aide on the landing bench), own business (the card put face down, the empty fourth chair facing all three, the clasp, Quenna counting the arrangements on her fingers on the half-landing), the "Coss had meant every word" orphan absorbed, the aide at the booth new. Coss's speech keeps the packet's order of points; its sentences are new. The ≥.50 hits are protected and brief-quoted lines plus three dialogue sentences. Residual: Quenna's second half-landing paragraph (80 words) still follows the source stair speech beat for beat — "I told a panel you'd be fact before anybody looked closely. You are fact. … He looked closely anyway. He thinks the category beats the fact. I put you in front of him, Cael. Whatever the next three weeks want from me, I'll give them." / source: "I staked my professional standing on the argument that you'd be established fact before anyone looked closely. You are established fact. … He looked closely anyway, and he's betting that fact loses to category. … I recruited you into this exposure, Cael. Whatever the next three weeks ask of me, they can have."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/recheck-r1.md:62:**ch44 scene 2 (breakup, Prynn's method, the tree, Karis with the lamp) — kept material as the brief allowed, two passages still track.** Prynn's method and the declaration tree were "keep" in the editorial review (16% then) and are unchanged in substance. The breakup paragraph is the editorial review's quoted ch44 example in varied form: "every one of them off to rearrange a life round something he had said in a room an hour ago" / "five people, redeploying their entire lives around a fifteen-year-old's insane sentence, because he had said it out loud and meant it", with the same five exits in the same order (~120 words). Karis's beat is re-set (out of the founding stacks with a lamp, not on the steps) but two of her three lines still track ("You keep saying that as though it might stop me." / "…as though it will discourage me."; the light seen twice before). Lighter item; see also §4 for the chronology defect this scene now carries.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/recheck-r1.md:68:**ch45 scene 3 (the schedule; re-touch) — acceptable.** Skeleton 7%; sentences rebuilt; the beat order is the source's, which for a reading-the-schedule scene is close to the only order. The editorial review's quoted ch45 example persists in varied form: "There had to be a page he had missed, in this building or in a records hall three districts away: an amendment, an annex, an order somewhere that made the flag lawful. Nothing ran for centuries on nothing. But things did, and he had seen them do it." / "Somewhere in this building, or in some Compact records hall three districts away, there had to be the page he'd missed — the amendment, the annex, the enabling order that made the flag legal. Systems did not run for four centuries on nothing. Except that they did." Then the circuit, the market interview, fourteen, custom in law's coat, in the source's order (~177 words). Lighter item; note only.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/recheck-r1.md:113:## 3. The three brief-quoted lines altered to clear the 8-word gate
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/recheck-r1.md:121:None of the three is BOOK_MAP-protected; no later book depends on their wording. The brief's "every brief-quoted line stays exact" and the 8-word gate cannot both be satisfied for an 8-word source run without a `protected-patterns.txt` entry, which is an owner's call, not a defect. My preference: restore line 2 exactly with a pattern entry (`This is your enrollment, not mine to trade`), keep 1 and 3 as they are. Not required for close.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/recheck-r1.md:141:**Protected lines (BOOK_MAP §9).** All verbatim: P15 (ch45); P17's language inside Quenna's record (ch46); "'Warden' was never a town title"; "You were fourteen." … "This is also the job."; "After that," said Quenna, "the job is to be right." (the source's own split); "New opponent. Four hundred pages, no tells, no third exchange."; Prynn's sixty-years line (words verbatim, see §3); Wray's D1 line; "Thank me if it works." P3 is echoed by Lira ("Whether you can not do it. In front of people who'd like you gone.") and not answered. Brief-quoted lines all exact except the three in §3; "I have never seen it survive." appears twice in ch42 (Coss, then Cael's retelling in italics) — fine.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/recheck-r1.md:151:1. **ch44 scene 1 (division of labour), ~900 words — rebuild from the event list.** This is the scene that still counts as skeleton paraphrase. The event list is fixed (Cael and Prynn take the code; Karis the founding shelves, truth not argument; Brom the witnesses, uncoached, the estate line; Naveth and Quenna procedure and lawful delay; Lira keeps him a fighter — "Not a lawyer wearing your face."). Handles the author already owns: let the claims come out of order and by interruption rather than round the desk (Lira first, not last, since she has been silent and furious; Brom's witness line said on the stair, not in the office); let the plan be made on Karis's ruled page, each name written as it is claimed, so the scene has an object; let Cael's "this was what he needed most" reflection be replaced by something he does (he writes Lira's hour into the page before his own). Keep every quoted line.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/recheck-r1.md:154:4. **ch46 scene 5, from "It held four." to "It's also the only true one I've got.", ~400 words.** Carry the page-as-page handle through: the four as four lines in his hand (name, century, order, days; three that stop; the fourth's eleven words counted, not quoted), and "how big it was" as a margin note rather than narration.
