editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/review-cold.md:13:**Where interest caught.** Immediately, at breakfast in 40: five terms counted on fingers, Brom adding "Buckets," and the cook's woodpile being called kindling. The experiment that follows is the best kind of fantasy-science scene: "Nothing glowed," then the ring of char and the thread of smoke "straight as a plumb line," and a cost that arrives *after*, cold down the arm, that nobody watching can see. Karis's "You haven't got fire. You've got a spark" is the sentence I would quote to someone to sell the book. Interest caught again at the bench in 41 (Denvash standing "in the passage in front of the real one"), and hardest at the gate in 42, where Coss is let in "because nothing about him was wrong."
